00:11:11,476 --> 00:11:12,351
Along the way,

282
00:11:12,351 --> 00:11:14,917
the company made decisions about what the

283
00:11:14,917 --> 00:11:15,980
car would not be.

284
00:11:16,160 --> 00:11:18,397
Top Gear says Moers did not want

285
00:11:18,397 --> 00:11:19,936
to race it at Le Mans,

286
00:11:19,936 --> 00:11:22,802
because he disliked spending heavily on a

287
00:11:22,802 --> 00:11:25,738
series using balance of performance rules.

288
00:11:25,918 --> 00:11:28,675
He also said he was not interested

289
00:11:28,675 --> 00:11:30,539
in a speed competition.

290
00:11:30,719 --> 00:11:33,660
Each decision narrowed the project and,

291
00:11:33,660 --> 00:11:34,791
by our reading,

292
00:11:34,791 --> 00:11:37,430
kept the delay from growing longer.

293
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:40,665
Top Gear's buying guide includes a warning

294
00:11:40,665 --> 00:11:43,550
from AMG about the original racing engine.

295
00:11:43,730 --> 00:11:46,030
It says the engine needs a team

296
00:11:46,030 --> 00:11:48,331
of experts to start and must be

297
00:11:48,331 --> 00:11:50,928
discarded after a handful of races.

298
00:11:51,108 --> 00:11:53,731
That is the source material the engineers

299
00:11:53,731 --> 00:11:53,987
had.

300
00:11:54,167 --> 00:11:56,606
Turning a part with that life into

301
00:11:56,606 --> 00:12:00,122
one that survives about fifty thousand kilometres

302
00:12:00,122 --> 00:12:02,059
of road use is a measure of

303
00:12:02,059 --> 00:12:03,351
the work involved.

304
00:12:03,700 --> 00:12:06,355
By our arithmetic we can express the

305
00:12:06,355 --> 00:12:08,124
improvement in one line.

306
00:12:08,304 --> 00:12:10,837
A road car engine that lasts fifty

307
00:12:10,837 --> 00:12:14,265
thousand kilometres is not a long-lived engine

308
00:12:14,265 --> 00:12:15,607
by road standards.

309
00:12:15,787 --> 00:12:18,219
But set against an engine that is

310
00:12:18,219 --> 00:12:20,799
discarded after a handful of races,

311
00:12:20,799 --> 00:12:22,126
it is a huge step.

312
00:12:22,306 --> 00:12:24,744
The delay bought durability as much as

313
00:12:24,744 --> 00:12:25,963
it bought legality.

314
00:12:26,143 --> 00:12:27,332
That is our reading,

315
00:12:27,332 --> 00:12:29,057
not a claim from the sources.

316
00:12:29,406 --> 00:12:32,260
One more detail about the source engine,

317
00:12:32,260 --> 00:12:34,329
because the sources disagree.

318
00:12:34,509 --> 00:12:37,504
Motor1's twenty eighteen report says it is

319
00:12:37,504 --> 00:12:40,286
based on the unit from Lewis Hamilton's

320
00:12:40,286 --> 00:12:42,497
twenty fifteen Formula One car.

321
00:12:42,677 --> 00:12:45,379
Wikipedia names the W oh six,

322
00:12:45,379 --> 00:12:47,523
the twenty fifteen car,

323
00:12:47,523 --> 00:12:49,573
through Ola Källenius.

324
00:12:49,753 --> 00:12:52,144
Autocar says it is adapted from the

325
00:12:52,144 --> 00:12:55,012
twenty seventeen championship-winning car.

326
00:12:55,192 --> 00:12:58,060
Two sources point to twenty fifteen and

327
00:12:58,060 --> 00:12:59,825
one to twenty seventeen.

328
00:13:00,174 --> 00:13:01,905
Why does the year matter for the

329
00:13:01,905 --> 00:13:02,229
delay?

330
00:13:02,409 --> 00:13:05,716
Because a Formula One engine develops every

331
00:13:05,716 --> 00:13:08,560
season, and a road car programme that

332
00:13:08,560 --> 00:13:11,482
starts from one version and ends years

333
00:13:11,482 --> 00:13:14,019
later is chasing a moving target.

334
00:13:14,199 --> 00:13:16,883
We cannot tell from the sources whether

335
00:13:16,883 --> 00:13:19,498
the engineers updated the design as it

336
00:13:19,498 --> 00:13:19,842
went.

337
00:13:20,022 --> 00:13:23,028
But the disagreement itself shows how hard

338
00:13:23,028 --> 00:13:25,318
it is to describe a project that

339
00:13:25,318 --> 00:13:25,676
long.

340
00:13:26,025 --> 00:13:28,873
Wikipedia lists what else the car had

341
00:13:28,873 --> 00:13:29,334
to do.

342
00:13:29,514 --> 00:13:31,687
Active front diffuser flaps,

343
00:13:31,687 --> 00:13:34,169
a two-part extendable rear wing,

344
00:13:34,169 --> 00:13:36,109
adjustable front louvres.

345
00:13:36,289 --> 00:13:39,551
Driving modes called Race Safe,

346
00:13:39,551 --> 00:13:40,604
Race, E V,

347
00:13:40,604 --> 00:13:44,393
Race Plus, Strat Two and Individual.

348
00:13:44,573 --> 00:13:47,248
Race Plus and Strat Two raise total

349
00:13:47,248 --> 00:13:49,542
downforce by up to five times.

350
00:13:49,722 --> 00:13:51,822
All of it had to be designed,

351
00:13:51,822 --> 00:13:54,284
tested and certified for the road.

352
00:13:54,634 --> 00:13:57,583
The body and chassis are carbon fibre,

353
00:13:57,583 --> 00:13:59,212
with butterfly doors,

354
00:13:59,212 --> 00:14:00,997
according to Wikipedia.

355
00:14:01,177 --> 00:14:03,523
Gorden Wagener, head of design,

356
00:14:03,523 --> 00:14:05,112
and Hartmut Sinkwitz,

357
00:14:05,112 --> 00:14:06,929
who led interior design,

358
00:14:06,929 --> 00:14:09,199
were responsible for the look.

359
00:14:09,379 --> 00:14:11,318
A show car can be anything.

360
00:14:11,498 --> 00:14:14,682
A production car must pass crash tests,

361
00:14:14,682 --> 00:14:18,355
fit people, keep them comfortable and survive

362
00:14:18,355 --> 00:14:19,416
years of use.

363
00:14:19,596 --> 00:14:22,615
That transition takes time in any programme.

364
00:14:22,964 --> 00:14:25,703
The scale of production was small,

365
00:14:25,703 --> 00:14:26,912
but not simple.

366
00:14:27,092 --> 00:14:30,538
Wikipedia says all two hundred seventy-five cars

367
00:14:30,538 --> 00:14:34,127
are hand-built, with production from August twenty

368
00:14:34,127 --> 00:14:36,496
twenty-two to twenty twenty-five.

369
00:14:36,676 --> 00:14:37,995
By our arithmetic,

370
00:14:37,995 --> 00:14:40,413
that is about three years for two

371
00:14:40,413 --> 00:14:42,318
hundred seventy-five cars,

372
00:14:42,318 --> 00:14:44,443
or around ninety cars a year.

373
00:14:44,623 --> 00:14:47,483
Hand-building at that rate means a long,

374
00:14:47,483 --> 00:14:49,557
careful process for each one.

375
00:14:49,907 --> 00:14:52,447
So even after the engine was solved,

376
00:14:52,447 --> 00:14:54,916
the full run could not be delivered

377
00:14:54,916 --> 00:14:55,480
at once.

378
00:14:55,660 --> 00:14:58,434
A customer who ordered in twenty seventeen

379
00:14:58,434 --> 00:15:00,877
might not have received the car until

380
00:15:00,877 --> 00:15:03,320
much later than the first delivery in

381
00:15:03,320 --> 00:15:05,169
January twenty twenty-three.

382
00:15:05,349 --> 00:15:07,039
We do not know the order of

383
00:15:07,039 --> 00:15:09,354
delivery, and the sources do not say.

384
00:15:09,534 --> 00:15:11,975
But production time adds to the wait

385
00:15:11,975 --> 00:15:13,331
for the last buyers.

386
00:15:13,680 --> 00:15:15,790
The AMG One was not the only

387
00:15:15,790 --> 00:15:17,372
hypercar to run late.

388
00:15:17,552 --> 00:15:20,609
Wikipedia says Aston Martin delivered only ten

389
00:15:20,609 --> 00:15:23,333
Valkyries in the fourth quarter of twenty

390
00:15:23,333 --> 00:15:25,393
twenty-one, fewer than planned,

391
00:15:25,393 --> 00:15:27,652
which caused it to miss its profit

392
00:15:27,652 --> 00:15:28,118
target.

393
00:15:28,298 --> 00:15:30,911
Autonews, citing unnamed sources,

394
00:15:30,911 --> 00:15:34,474
said electronics problems delayed the launch.

395
00:15:34,654 --> 00:15:37,640
Fortune said the launch was delayed repeatedly

396
00:15:37,640 --> 00:15:40,041
while the carmaker fixed electronics.

397
00:15:40,392 --> 00:15:42,539
The difference is in the explanation.

398
00:15:42,719 --> 00:15:43,916
For the AMG One,

399
00:15:43,916 --> 00:15:47,580
executives named the problems and described them,

400
00:15:47,580 --> 00:15:50,347
and the sources agree on the details.

401
00:15:50,527 --> 00:15:51,892
For the Valkyrie,

402
00:15:51,892 --> 00:15:54,863
our sources give less detail and rely

403
00:15:54,863 --> 00:15:56,309
on unnamed people.

404
00:15:56,489 --> 00:15:58,857
That does not mean one project was

405
00:15:58,857 --> 00:15:59,902
better managed.

406
00:16:00,082 --> 00:16:01,032
It means that,

407
00:16:01,032 --> 00:16:02,118
for the AMG One,

408
00:16:02,118 --> 00:16:04,221
we can tell you much more about

409
00:16:04,221 --> 00:16:05,307
why it was late.

410
00:16:05,657 --> 00:16:07,951
Hypercars are late often enough that it

411
00:16:07,951 --> 00:16:09,186
looks like a pattern.

412
00:16:09,366 --> 00:16:12,119
The most radical cars take the most

413
00:16:12,119 --> 00:16:15,737
development, and radical means new technology,

414
00:16:15,737 --> 00:16:18,805
new regulations and untested packaging.

415
00:16:18,985 --> 00:16:21,692
A manufacturer that promises a date is

416
00:16:21,692 --> 00:16:22,974
making a forecast,

417
00:16:22,974 --> 00:16:24,256
not a measurement.

418
00:16:24,436 --> 00:16:26,248
In the AMG One's case,

419
00:16:26,248 --> 00:16:28,720
the forecast was off by years,

420
00:16:28,720 --> 00:16:31,274
and the company said so openly.

421
00:16:31,623 --> 00:16:34,421
Consider the timing from the customers' side.

422
00:16:34,601 --> 00:16:37,575
Someone who ordered in twenty seventeen was

423
00:16:37,575 --> 00:16:39,443
told early twenty nineteen.

424
00:16:39,623 --> 00:16:41,911
In twenty nineteen they were told early

425
00:16:41,911 --> 00:16:42,967
twenty twenty-one.

426
00:16:43,147 --> 00:16:45,759
Later they were told twenty twenty-two.

427
00:16:45,939 --> 00:16:48,906
Each message came with an explanation and,

428
00:16:48,906 --> 00:16:50,248
according to Moers,

429
00:16:50,248 --> 00:16:51,802
no attempt to hide it.

430
00:16:51,982 --> 00:16:53,031
By our reading,

431
00:16:53,031 --> 00:16:55,827
honesty is what made the wait tolerable,

432
00:16:55,827 --> 00:16:58,274
because the order book stayed full.

433
00:16:58,624 --> 00:17:00,946
And the order book did stay full.

434
00:17:01,126 --> 00:17:03,784
Wikipedia says more than four times as

435
00:17:03,784 --> 00:17:06,512
many orders arrived as there were cars,

436
00:17:06,512 --> 00:17:09,170
and that Mercedes refused to raise the

437
00:17:09,170 --> 00:17:09,590
limit.

438
00:17:09,770 --> 00:17:12,189
Our sources show no sign that the

439
00:17:12,189 --> 00:17:14,755
company cut its price or added cars

440
00:17:14,755 --> 00:17:16,295
to keep buyers happy.

441
00:17:16,475 --> 00:17:18,067
For a delayed product,

442
00:17:18,067 --> 00:17:19,225
that is unusual,

443
00:17:19,225 --> 00:17:21,974
and it suggests how much people wanted

444
00:17:21,974 --> 00:17:23,638
this particular engine.

445
00:17:23,988 --> 00:17:26,699
If you are thinking about a limited

446
00:17:26,699 --> 00:17:28,868
car, the AMG One story has a

447
00:17:28,868 --> 00:17:29,410
lesson.

448
00:17:29,590 --> 00:17:32,327
A delivery date in an early report

449
00:17:32,327 --> 00:17:33,131
is a hope.

450
00:17:33,311 --> 00:17:36,234
A specification in an early report is

451
00:17:36,234 --> 00:17:36,945
a target.

452
00:17:37,125 --> 00:17:38,222
Both can move,

453
00:17:38,222 --> 00:17:40,260
and in this case both did.

454
00:17:40,440 --> 00:17:42,508
The only things that did not move

455
00:17:42,508 --> 00:17:44,577
were the price of about two point

456
00:17:44,577 --> 00:17:46,896
seven million dollars and the number,

457
00:17:46,896 --> 00:17:48,462
two hundred seventy-five.

458
00:17:48,812 --> 00:17:51,083
And the owners who waited gained something

459
00:17:51,083 --> 00:17:52,597
that cannot be bought later.

460
00:17:52,777 --> 00:17:55,579
Mercedes has, according to Motor1,

461
00:17:55,579 --> 00:17:58,710
ruled out putting a Formula One engine

462
00:17:58,710 --> 00:18:00,440
in a future road car.

463
00:18:00,620 --> 00:18:02,741
Whatever you think of the delay,

464
00:18:02,741 --> 00:18:04,729
the car that arrived is a rare

465
00:18:04,729 --> 00:18:06,651
thing, built at a time when a

466
00:18:06,651 --> 00:18:08,573
company still tried to do it.

467
00:18:08,753 --> 00:18:10,872
That is a fair reason to forgive

468
00:18:10,872 --> 00:18:11,667
a few years.

469
00:18:12,016 --> 00:18:14,564
The most interesting evidence is what the

470
00:18:14,564 --> 00:18:15,558
executives said.

471
00:18:15,738 --> 00:18:18,315
Tobias Moers told Top Gear in September

472
00:18:18,315 --> 00:18:20,958
twenty nineteen that there was no excuse

473
00:18:20,958 --> 00:18:22,412
on the company's side,

474
00:18:22,412 --> 00:18:25,385
and that it maybe underestimated the journey.

475
00:18:25,565 --> 00:18:27,599
He said the final engine had been

476
00:18:27,599 --> 00:18:29,757
specified and was on a dynamometer.

477
00:18:29,937 --> 00:18:31,766
It is rare to hear a company

478
00:18:31,766 --> 00:18:33,791
admit it underestimated a task.

479
00:18:34,141 --> 00:18:36,838
Ola Källenius, according to CarAdvice,

480
00:18:36,838 --> 00:18:39,250
joked that he was sure the company

481
00:18:39,250 --> 00:18:41,165
was drunk when it said yes.

482
00:18:41,345 --> 00:18:44,109
He said the idea was pitched about

483
00:18:44,109 --> 00:18:46,465
four years before the reveal.

484
00:18:46,645 --> 00:18:47,423
It is a joke,

485
00:18:47,423 --> 00:18:48,979
and should be read as one.

486
00:18:49,159 --> 00:18:51,689
But there is real information in it:

487
00:18:51,689 --> 00:18:54,710
the project was approved before the company

488
00:18:54,710 --> 00:18:57,240
understood how much work was needed.

489
00:18:57,589 --> 00:19:00,481
Moers also said he expected a period

490
00:19:00,481 --> 00:19:02,890
of major issues that had to be

491
00:19:02,890 --> 00:19:03,452
solved.

492
00:19:03,632 --> 00:19:05,988
That tells us the engineers knew from

493
00:19:05,988 --> 00:19:08,217
the start that a Formula One engine

494
00:19:08,217 --> 00:19:09,554
would not simply fit.

495
00:19:09,734 --> 00:19:11,159
They just did not know how long

496
00:19:11,159 --> 00:19:12,079
the work would take.

497
00:19:12,259 --> 00:19:13,366
By our reading,

498
00:19:13,366 --> 00:19:15,653
that is the heart of the delay:

499
00:19:15,653 --> 00:19:16,834
a known problem,

500
00:19:16,834 --> 00:19:18,679
with an unknown schedule.

501
00:19:19,029 --> 00:19:21,598
Judge the result by what the sources

502
00:19:21,598 --> 00:19:21,955
list.

503
00:19:22,135 --> 00:19:25,102
All two hundred seventy-five cars sold,

504
00:19:25,102 --> 00:19:27,613
with more than four times as many

505
00:19:27,613 --> 00:19:29,972
orders, according to Wikipedia.

506
00:19:30,152 --> 00:19:32,619
A Nürburgring lap of six minutes,

507
00:19:32,619 --> 00:19:36,208
twenty-nine point zero nine seconds in September

508
00:19:36,208 --> 00:19:37,629
twenty twenty-four.

509
00:19:37,809 --> 00:19:42,000
Production-car records at Monza and other circuits.

510
00:19:42,180 --> 00:19:44,179
A car that can be driven on

511
00:19:44,179 --> 00:19:46,919
public roads, with a plug-in range of

512
00:19:46,919 --> 00:19:48,844
about eighteen kilometres.

513
00:19:49,194 --> 00:19:51,587
The customers who waited did get the

514
00:19:51,587 --> 00:19:51,853
car.

515
00:19:52,033 --> 00:19:55,235
The first delivery on the sixteenth of

516
00:19:55,235 --> 00:19:58,942
January twenty twenty-three came in a livery

517
00:19:58,942 --> 00:20:01,723
inspired by the Formula One car W

518
00:20:01,723 --> 00:20:03,492
twelve E Performance.

519
00:20:03,672 --> 00:20:04,868
By our arithmetic,

520
00:20:04,868 --> 00:20:07,126
it came more than five years after

521
00:20:07,126 --> 00:20:09,849
the Frankfurt reveal in twenty seventeen.

522
00:20:10,198 --> 00:20:12,250
The price of the delay was paid

523
00:20:12,250 --> 00:20:14,633
by the company's schedule and by the

524
00:20:14,633 --> 00:20:15,957
customers' patience.

525
00:20:16,137 --> 00:20:18,008
The price of the solution,

526
00:20:18,008 --> 00:20:20,312
the engine's short service life,

527
00:20:20,312 --> 00:20:21,896
is paid by the owners.

528
00:20:22,076 --> 00:20:24,981
Wikipedia says the engine must be returned

529
00:20:24,981 --> 00:20:28,647
for refurbishment at about fifty thousand kilometres.

530
00:20:28,827 --> 00:20:30,957
A road car that needs that is

531
00:20:30,957 --> 00:20:33,894
the final consequence of making a racing

532
00:20:33,894 --> 00:20:35,363
engine street legal.

533
00:20:35,713 --> 00:20:37,729
So why did it take years longer

534
00:20:37,729 --> 00:20:38,639
than promised?

535
00:20:38,819 --> 00:20:41,591
Because a Formula One engine had to

536
00:20:41,591 --> 00:20:42,700
learn to idle,

537
00:20:42,700 --> 00:20:44,838
pass emissions, stay quiet,

538
00:20:44,838 --> 00:20:47,372
and live inside a hybrid system,

539
00:20:47,372 --> 00:20:48,323
all at once,

540
00:20:48,323 --> 00:20:50,857
in a car that people would drive

541
00:20:50,857 --> 00:20:52,124
on public roads.

542
00:20:52,304 --> 00:20:54,446
Every one of those was solved,

543
00:20:54,446 --> 00:20:56,159
and every one took time.

544
00:20:56,339 --> 00:20:57,787
That is the whole story,

545
00:20:57,787 --> 00:20:59,415
and the sources support it.

546
00:20:59,765 --> 00:21:01,205
A last caution.

547
00:21:01,385 --> 00:21:03,639
We have not driven the car,

548
00:21:03,639 --> 00:21:06,977
and the early specifications in the 2018

549
00:21:06,977 --> 00:21:09,147
reports were expectations,

550
00:21:09,147 --> 00:21:10,232
not promises.

551
00:21:10,412 --> 00:21:12,385
We have tried to show where the

552
00:21:12,385 --> 00:21:14,612
sources agree, where they disagree,

553
00:21:14,612 --> 00:21:16,903
and where our own arithmetic fills a

554
00:21:16,903 --> 00:21:17,157
gap.

555
00:21:17,337 --> 00:21:19,154
If you know a firsthand account,

556
00:21:19,154 --> 00:21:20,516
tell us in the comments,

557
00:21:20,516 --> 00:21:21,935
with where it comes from.

558
00:21:22,284 --> 00:21:25,081
In the other videos of this series,

559
00:21:25,081 --> 00:21:28,198
we reveal two secrets hidden inside the

560
00:21:28,198 --> 00:21:30,915
AMG One, compare it with the Aston

561
00:21:30,915 --> 00:21:33,952
Martin Valkyrie, and count the cost of

562
00:21:33,952 --> 00:21:36,669
